            "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef main():\n    # Load the vectors as float64 for high numerical precision\n    X = np.load(\"vectors.npy\").astype(np.float64)\n    n_vectors = X.shape[0]\n\n    # Precompute squared norms of each vector\n    sq_norms = np.sum(X**2, axis=1)\n\n    # Compute the Gram matrix G = X @ X.T via optimized BLAS GEMM\n    G = X @ X.T\n\n    total_distance = 0.0\n    step = 1000\n\n    # Process in chunks to maintain low memory footprint and cache efficiency\n    for i in range(0, n_vectors, step):\n        end = min(i + step, n_vectors)\n        chunk_len = end - i\n\n        # Compute squared Euclidean distances: ||x_i - x_j||^2 = ||x_i||^2 + ||x_j||^2 - 2<x_i, x_j>\n        d2 = sq_norms[i:end, None] + sq_norms[None, :] - 2.0 * G[i:end]\n        np.maximum(d2, 0.0, out=d2)\n\n        # Explicitly zero out the diagonal entries (distance from vector to itself)\n        diag_rows = np.arange(chunk_len)\n        diag_cols = np.arange(i, end)\n        d2[diag_rows, diag_cols] = 0.0\n\n        # Compute Euclidean distance\n        np.sqrt(d2, out=d2)\n        total_distance += float(np.sum(d2))\n\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total_distance}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
